  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Sarmutoside and Acyl-CoA hydrolase through a multi-step pathway. Sarmutoside is directly linked to PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, which is then targeted by Lehualide A. Lehualide A, in turn, has a target of Acyl-CoA hydrolase. This indicates that Sarmutoside may act through Lehualide A to influence Acyl-CoA hydrolase. Additionally, Sarmutoside is also connected to another compound, 2-(3,4-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5,6-Dihydroxy-7-Methoxychromen-4-One, which also targets Acyl-CoA hydrolase. The scores for these relationships are relatively high, suggesting a plausible biological interaction. However, the exact mechanism by which Sarmutoside affects Acyl-CoA hydrolase remains unclear, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the role of these compounds in the pathway.",
